ANNOTATION: "SEP-KMAC-NO-HW-APP: the KMAC hardware application interface has no requester in SEP. hw/sys/sep/rtl/kmac_wrapper.sv:186 ties .app_i('0) on the kmac instance and :187 leaves .app_o unconnected, so app_req.req_valid is constant 0 and the FSM can never leave StIdle toward StAppCfg. Excluded: the StApp* FSM arms (543-679), the set_appid / clr_appid session-configuration latch (326-337), the SelApp and SelOutLen arms of the message mux (993-1012), the app digest assembly (1226-1236) and the StApp* arm of the key mux (1306-1313). NOT excluded: the StError* and StTerminalError arms (702-832), because StErrorKeyNotValid is also entered from StSw (kmac_app.sv:847-849), and the kstrength-dependent state masking and digest sizing (1113-1118, 1150-1163), which software reaches through CFG_SHADOWED."
